<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elazığ</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Elaziz, Mamuret-ul-Aziz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elazığ is a city in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, on a plain east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>. It was founded in the 19th century below the old fortress town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harput">Harput</a> and named Mamuret-ul-Aziz after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Abdulaziz. In ancient times its plain was the heart of the kingdom of Isuwa and later of Sophene, and many sites were excavated before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keban-dam">Keban Dam</a> flooded part of it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elazig.jpg" alt="Elazığ" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Taha Koçak · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elaz%C4%B1%C4%9F_City_Center.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
